# Documented exceptions for AUT-1464 Trivy scanning. Only add a CVE here
# after confirming no fixed version exists anywhere (not just "not yet
# upgraded") — see git history / PR discussion on AUT-1464 for the
# investigation behind each entry.

# python-ecdsa: Minerva timing attack on the P-256 curve. No fix planned —
# maintainers have declared pure-Python timing-attack fixes out of scope.
# Pulled in transitively via python-jose for JWT auth. Real exposure is
# conditional: only exercised if JWT_ALGORITHM=ES256 is ever configured
# (see src/autobots/auth/security.py). Proper fix is migrating off
# python-jose/ecdsa to an OpenSSL-backed JWT library, not a version bump —
# tracked separately.
CVE-2024-23342

# chromadb: pre-authentication code injection via trust_remote_code on the
# /api/v2/.../collections endpoint. No patched version exists yet — even
# the latest chromadb release is listed as vulnerable. Lower risk here
# since this repo only uses chromadb.HttpClient as a client against an
# external CHROMA_HOST; it does not run the vulnerable chromadb server
# component itself.
CVE-2026-45829
